#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105411 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e598ad1e-cee5-5d5f-b2a9-c067e4625cf6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Angles and Magnitudes"}] :question/id #uuid "1a24b403-754c-5424-8182-8cad3487deed" :question/math-academy-id "e-15606" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=13$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\, | \\cos   \\theta \\\\  & = 13 \\cos   ( \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} ) \\\\  & = 13 \\cdot  ( - \\frac{1}{2} ) \\\\  & = - \\frac{13}{2} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105412 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91691448-c59a-56dc-a775-d4e9c3297036" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "da8a1521-86cc-5747-88a7-e2ec56010c11" :question/math-academy-id "e-15607" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |} \\\\  & = \\frac{{a}_{x} {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} {b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2} + {b}_{y}^{2} + {b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{3 \\cdot  2 + 3 \\cdot  ( - 7 ) + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 7 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51e317c-f6b3-5704-afb4-bdfc79f1176f" :knowledge-point/title "Projecting a Vector Onto a Perpendicular Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "4693b28f-df75-574e-8e49-bb89e162b107" :question/math-academy-id "e-15608" :question/problem "Let \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ - 4 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |} \\\\  & = \\frac{{a}_{x} {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} {b}_{y} + {c}_{z} {b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2} + {b}_{y}^{2} + {b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{0 \\cdot  2 + 0 \\cdot  ( - 4 ) + 1 \\cdot  0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = 0.\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91691448-c59a-56dc-a775-d4e9c3297036" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "846fec6b-0634-527c-95c2-25754ce33c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102376} {:answer/id #uuid "98084e96-1175-5ccb-9f1b-d2c905265afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102377} {:answer/id #uuid "cda2fdc1-166a-5b7a-b0ce-a12be6fe892a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102378} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd1d530-3fe4-537c-8416-40b990c1ef12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102379} {:answer/id #uuid "22d7a360-bc93-5f42-9551-0ca7a207abd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cda2fdc1-166a-5b7a-b0ce-a12be6fe892a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102378} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6ff4f7-e72a-5c98-af10-7d1e281c3900" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e48bd53-4841-5a1d-adee-85eb3b590727" :question/math-academy-id "q-18374" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{p} = \\langle  \\sqrt{2} , 1 , - 1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{q} = \\langle  \\sqrt{8} , - \\sqrt{3} , 1 \\rangle  .$. Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}+1\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51e317c-f6b3-5704-afb4-bdfc79f1176f" :knowledge-point/title "Projecting a Vector Onto a Perpendicular Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e91d1d3b-1185-52e5-a2b0-ca758b020b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e91d1d3b-1185-52e5-a2b0-ca758b020b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275292} :answer-field/id #uuid "825cc115-7959-55bc-9a6d-6100726bc4e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1067d56-4d83-5281-8c53-6dfcd93ed0f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-275256" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot x+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2x+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 2x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-8 \\\\ x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e598ad1e-cee5-5d5f-b2a9-c067e4625cf6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Angles and Magnitudes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52455008-c333-5dd1-92b4-72b4768f2da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52455008-c333-5dd1-92b4-72b4768f2da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275295} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec7d6cad-97ac-539c-a22f-fd918e59492a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4153b8de-c0c0-52e9-920b-bb4a1839c543" :question/math-academy-id "q-318971" :question/problem "Suppose $|\\,r\\,|=10$ and the angle between vectors $r$ and $s$ is $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r & =|\\,r\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10cos\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
